---
Use `http://127.0.0.1:8000` for the server in the
[LLMD quickstart]($link.page('llmd/quickstart')). A client that accepts an
OpenAI-compatible base URL uses `http://127.0.0.1:8000/v1`. For a remote
deployment, use its base URL and any authentication it requires.

The endpoint examples in this reference are source-reviewed. Verification
against a running LLMD instance is pending.

# [List the loaded model]($heading.id('list-the-loaded-model'))

`GET /v1/models` returns the model served by this LLMD instance in `data`.

```sh
curl -fsS http://127.0.0.1:8000/v1/models
```

# [Read the model ID]($heading.id('read-the-model-id'))

Use `data[0].id` as the `model` field in a
[chat completion]($link.page('llmd/api/chat-completions').ref('create-a-chat-completion')).
The CLI's `--model-name` sets the ID. When omitted, LLMD uses the basename
of `--model`. Start a server with a different checkpoint to serve a different
model. See [Checkpoint storage]($link.page('llmd/quickstart').ref('checkpoint-storage'))
for model sources and downloads.

# [Check service health and errors]($heading.id('check-service-health-and-errors'))

| Endpoint | Behavior |
| --- | --- |
| `GET /health` | Returns `OK` from the running HTTP service. Send an inference request supported by the loaded model to confirm it can answer. |
| `GET /metrics` | Exposes Prometheus metrics. See [Operations]($link.page('operations')). |

For errors from a chat request, see [Chat completion errors]($link.page('llmd/api/chat-completions').ref('errors')).
